# littlefs on Linux

Linux's own littlefs: the pinned checkout vendor.sh provisions in upstream/,
the project-owned adapter.c over it, and platform.linux.fs.littlefs, the
provider the Linux SDKs bind for mm.fs.littlefs. mm.build compiles lfs.c,
lfs_util.c, and the adapter -- the adapter with warnings as errors -- for a
program that reaches the provider, and links them into it.

It is independent of the Pico path, platforms/pico/sdk/pico-sdk/littlefs,
which the Pico SDK bridge compiles: its own pin, its own adapter, its own
provider, so either can change without the other. Both start at littlefs
v2.11.3, commit 6cb4e86540eca0d9ba62500a298385c9d863c8be, BSD-3-Clause;
mm.fs.conformance checks both against one contract. The adapter's ABI is
prefixed mm_linux_lfs_ where the Pico one's is mm_pico_lfs_, so a symbol
never names the wrong platform.
